'''Tal''' is an [[Afroasiatic languages|Afroasiatic]] language spoken in [[Plateau State]], [[Nigeria]].<ref name=e18/> Tal is spoken in a cluster of 53 villages located east of the [[Panyam]]-[[Shendam]] road. There are 6 dialects of Tal, namely Bongmuut, Buzuk, Nbaal, Muɗak, Muɗong, and Takong.<ref name="Blench2017">Blench, Roger. 2017. [https://www.academia.edu/35507157/CURRENT_RESEARCH_ON_THE_A3_WEST_CHADIC_LANGUAGES Current research on the A3 West Chadic languages].</ref>

